--- body ---
## Question

How often does a harness worker cross 100K prompt tokens, and what share of
worker spend is billed above that line? Haiku 5.5 is five times dearer per
token past 100K prompt tokens (`skills/route/routes.json`); [[1114]] builds
decomposition machinery only if the cliff is actually crossed.

## Data

- Claude Code traces under `~/.claude/projects/` on doudou and padme, main
  sessions and subagents. `scripts/trace-stats.py` already parses them, one
  row per agent, usage counted once per `message.id` (tickets 0236, 0237).
- Pi sessions (`~/.pi/agent/sessions/`) and Codex rollouts
  (`~/.codex/sessions/`) for the headless seats, where their usage records
  allow it.
- Arena legs N (Haiku 5.5) and L (Luna @medium): file the arena-side part in
  the arena repository if its run records are needed.

## Method

Prompt size of one call = `input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens +
cache_creation_input_tokens`. Per agent: peak prompt size, number of calls
past 85K and past 100K, cost as billed, and the counterfactual cost had every
call been billed at the under-cliff rate. Report by model, role (main session
vs subagent vs headless seat) and project, over a stated window.

Extend `trace-stats.py` (new columns, tiered pricing for Haiku 5.5) rather
than writing a parallel parser; check its PRICING table against current list
prices first, since it is dated 2026-06.

## Decision rule (pre-registered)

1114 continues if, among Haiku-eligible workers (subagents and headless
seats), more than 10% peak above 85K, or more than 10% of their spend is
billed above 100K. Otherwise 1114 closes as a documented non-finding, and
the existing one-line rule in the route skill stands.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `trace-stats.py` emits peak prompt size, calls past 85K and 100K, and
      over-cliff spend per agent, with tests on a fixture trace that crosses
      the cliff
- [ ] Haiku 5.5 tiered pricing in its PRICING table, source and date cited
- [ ] Run on doudou and padme over the last 30 days; summary committed
      under `docs/` (aggregates only, no transcript content)
- [ ] Decision recorded in the logs of this ticket and of [[1114]]
- [ ] `make check` passes
